  "question": {
    "text": "Four charges equal to \\(-Q\\) are placed at the four corners of a square and a charge \\(q\\) is at its centre. If the system is in equilibrium, the value of \\(q\\) is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "w4eKR",
      "text": "\\(\\frac{-Q}{4}(1+2 \\sqrt{2})\\)",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JyXrX",
      "text": "\\(\\frac{Q}{4}(1+2 \\sqrt{2})\\)",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "TzJGg",
      "text": "\\(\\frac{-\\mathrm{Q}}{2}(1+2 \\sqrt{2})\\)",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "G0zxe",
      "text": "\\(\\frac{\\mathrm{Q}}{2}(1+2 \\sqrt{2})\\)",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Hints: <img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/wbjee/ILPZc5J7uIBT9A8mpTsNINXnqU9PCO7FoGsg_eXZ_Yk.original.fullsize.png\"><br>\n\\(\\begin{aligned} & \\mathrm{F}^{\\prime}=\\sqrt{2} \\mathrm{~F}+\\frac{\\mathrm{F}}{2}=\\mathrm{F}\\left(\\sqrt{2}+\\frac{1}{2}\\right) \\\\ & \\frac{\\mathrm{q} Q}{\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{2} \\mathrm{a}}{2}\\right)^2}=\\frac{\\mathrm{Q}^2}{\\mathrm{a}^2}\\left(\\sqrt{2}+\\frac{1}{2}\\right), \\mathrm{q}=\\frac{\\mathrm{Q}}{2}\\left(\\frac{2 \\sqrt{2}+1}{2}\\right) \\\\ & q=\\frac{Q}{4}(2 \\sqrt{2}+1)\\end{aligned}\\)",
    "image": null
